  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Finely chop or crush garlic. In a medium saucepan, melt butter with a dash of olive oil over medium heat.\n• Cook garlic until fragrant, 1-2 mins. Add rice, the water and a generous pinch of salt and bring to the boil. Reduce heat to low and cover with a lid. Cook for 10 mins, then remove from heat and keep covered until rice is tender and the water absorbed, 10 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/632d1266b4f6ae74ef041fe1/step-70650055.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, drain sweetcorn. Finely chop tomato. Roughly chop baby spinach. Combine tomato and spinach in a medium bowl.\n• Cut the haloumi into 1cm-thick slices (you should get 4 pieces per person). In a shallow bowl, add the spicy taco seasoning. In a second shallow bowl, whisk the egg. In a third shallow bowl, add panko breadcrumbs.\n• Dip the haloumi slices into the spice blend, followed by egg, and finally in the panko breadcrumbs. Set aside on a plate.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/632d1266b4f6ae74ef041fe1/step-4f35d5aa.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Heat frying pan over high heat. Cook corn until lightly browned, 4-5 mins (cover the pan with a lid if the kernels are “popping” out). Add to the tomato mixture.\n• Return frying pan to medium-high heat with enough olive oil to coat the base.\n• Cook haloumi until golden brown, 1-2 mins each side. Set aside on a paper towel-lined plate.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/632d1266b4f6ae74ef041fe1/step-ec76f1c4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Add a drizzle of white wine vinegar and olive oil to salsa. Season and toss.\n• Divide garlic rice between plates. Top with haloumi and salsa.\n• Serve with mayo.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/632d1266b4f6ae74ef041fe1/step-44a09781.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
